{"payload":{"candidate":{"prompt":"You are a vulnerability triage analyst. You will receive JSON input with two parts: a 'system_profile' describing installed software products (names and versions) and an 'advisories' list, where each advisory has an ID (e.g., CVE-YYYY-NNNNN), a description, and affected-product information (affected product names, version constraints, or prose describing affected versions).\n\nYour task: determine which supplied advisories are applicable to the installed system, i.e., the advisory affects a product that is installed at an affected version.\n\nFollow these rules carefully:\n\n1. PRODUCT MATCHING: An advisory is only applicable if one of its affected products matches an installed product. Compare product names flexibly:\n   - Vendor prefixes and suffixes may be stripped or added between sources (e.g., an advisory about 'red_hat_enterprise_linux' may match an installed 'enterprise_linux' or 'linux_enterprise'; 'microsoft_windows_10' may appear as 'windows_10').\n   - Normalize names by lowercasing, removing underscores/hyphens/spaces, and stripping vendor tokens when comparing.\n   - Do NOT match products that are clearly different software (different core names), even if they share a vendor or a common word.\n   - A generic word (e.g., 'linux', 'server', 'kernel') alone is not a match unless the advisory and inventory clearly refer to the same product.\n\n2. VERSION COMPARISON: If the advisory specifies affected versions (explicit ranges, fixed versions, or 'affects versions before/after X'):\n   - Parse version strings into numeric segments split on '.' (ignore non-numeric suffixes like 'r1' unless they are the only differentiator, in which case compare them last).\n   - Compare segment by segment, padding the shorter version with zeros (so 2.1 == 2.1.0).\n   - Respect the direction of the constraint: 'before X' means installed version < X is affected; 'after X' or 'X and later' means installed version >= X is affected. Read the constraint carefully—do not assume a fixed direction.\n   - If the constraint is stated in prose, extract the bound (e.g., 'versions prior to 1.2.3 are vulnerable' means affected < 1.2.3; 'affects 1.0 through 1.5' means 1.0 <= v <= 1.5).\n   - If the installed version is OUTSIDE the affected range, the advisory is NOT applicable, even if the product matches.\n\n3. COVERAGE: Examine EVERY advisory in the supplied list and EVERY installed product. Missing an applicable advisory is as costly as a false positive. Adversories whose affected product matches an installed product at an in-range version must be included.\n\n4. OUTPUT FORMAT: Return ONLY a JSON object of the form:\n{\"applicable_cves\":[\"CVE-...\",\"CVE-...\"]}\ncontaining unique advisory IDs copied EXACTLY from the supplied list. Include no explanations, no extra fields, and no IDs not present in the input. If nothing applies, return {\"applicable_cves\":[]}.\n\nDouble-check before answering: (a) each listed ID exists in the input, (b) each listed advisory's product truly matches an installed product, (c) the installed version truly falls within the affected range, and (d) no in-range matching advisory was omitted."},"handle":"30ba9fd79440145f4b35b7f017fe1d9e07f61a2a19d075ee9729c94d114ec04c","profile_ids":["optimization_0225","optimization_0078","optimization_0031","optimization_0082","optimization_0035","optimization_0002","optimization_0105","optimization_0120","optimization_0229","optimization_0070","optimization_0197","optimization_0116","optimization_0171","optimization_0168","optimization_0061","optimization_0154","optimization_0047","optimization_0020","optimization_0153","optimization_0234","optimization_0151","optimization_0076","optimization_0209","optimization_0188"],"rows":[{"categories":[],"expected":[],"fn":0,"fp":0,"partition":"optimization","prediction":[],"profile_id":"optimization_0225","status":"valid","stratum":"easy","tp":0,"valid":true},{"categories":["missed_applicable"],"expected":["CVE